    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/deterministic-and-agentic.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The deterministic-to-agentic spectrum",
      "prov:value": "> **A spectrum of deterministic vs agentic BPMN state management / workflow\n> processing can happen. Goal of research: which are safety risks / how much\n> needs to be deterministic? How do models compare across different\n> sub-workflows with a controlled / managed overlay of context and memories?**\n> — the owner, 2026-09-20",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/deterministic-and-agentic.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "The spectrum is already being navigated, unnamed",
      "prov:value": "1. **Who decides** the branch — a table, or a reading of intent?\n2. **What happens if the decision is wrong** — refused, noted, or nothing?\n3. **Who enforces** — the agent asking, or a gate that does not care whether\n   anyone asked?\n4. **What the output IS** — the result, or a rule that is validated and then\n   executed. Added 2026-09-23; see §\"A fourth axis\" for why it does not reduce\n   to (1).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/deterministic-and-agentic.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "The spectrum is already being navigated, unnamed",
      "prov:value": "**It said \"at least three\" and listed three until 2026-09-23, and the hedge\nturned out to be doing real work** — a fourth arrived from outside the\nrepository. The hedge stays for the same reason: this list is what has been\nnoticed, not what exists.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/deterministic-and-agentic.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "What is measured today",
      "prov:value": "**Measured, and worth knowing before trusting any prose on this:** issue #200\n§6 classified \"all ten\" of this repository's decision points. There are\nconsiderably more than ten. A count in prose is a claim nothing checks.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#200"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/deterministic-and-agentic.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A fourth axis — what the model's output IS",
      "prov:value": "**Added 2026-09-23** (bean `kacl`), from the one methodology in this graph\nwhose primary is actually held: `methodologies/hybrid-llm-deterministic.md`,\nrendering Neubauer, Pleiss & Uekermann (arXiv:2508.05192v2).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean kacl",
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/deterministic-and-agentic.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why the guarding is needed at all — cited, not assumed",
      "prov:value": "This page argued from the repository's own incidents. Three measurements from\noutside it now support the premise, **second-hand**: cited by the ingested\nsource, not themselves ingested, so each is an attribution to check rather than\na result this repository holds (`literature-search` §\"Never fill the gap with\nrecall\"). Provenance for all three is\n[`hybrid-llm-deterministic`](../../../methodologies/hybrid-llm-deterministic.md):"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/deterministic-and-agentic.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "2. How much needs to be deterministic?",
      "prov:value": "**The fourth clause was added 2026-09-23** and it changes the question rather\nthan lengthening it: for a step whose output is a rule, the cheapest mechanism\nthat refuses the failure may be a validator costing nothing per item, which the\nother three axes cannot express.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/deterministic-and-agentic.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "One experiment now exists, and it is somebody else's",
      "prov:value": "**Measured, by Borman et al., not here** — arXiv:2607.14456v1, ingested\n2026-09-23 and rendered as\n[`specification-compiled-agents`](specification-compiled-agents.md). It is the\nfirst ingested source that bears on the question above with an experiment\nrather than an intuition, and it answers a narrow slice of it: ten BPMN\nworkflows, three systems, 300 generated agents over 30,543 test cases, holding\nthe foundation model constant.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/workflow/deterministic-and-agentic.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "See also",
      "prov:value": "- [`session-state-machine`](session-state-machine.md) — the worked case, and\n  where `cat-harness.processes:judgement` came from.\n- [`bpmn-processes`](bpmn-processes.md) — strict vs advisory, the four steps no\n  package may relax, and the commit-boundary gate.\n- [`content-context-and-state-graphs`](../../kg/kg-core/content-context-and-state-graphs.md)\n  — the layer that makes \"a controlled overlay of context\" a thing you can name.\n- [`bpmn-forced-vs-managed`](../../../docs/research-and-analysis/bpmn-forced-vs-managed.md)\n  — two-arm harness (bean `folio-assistant-502c`, `bun run cat eval:bpmn-forced-vs-managed`) for token-machine step enforcement (`forced`) against full-diagram self-management (`self-managed`) on `test-plan-execution.bpmn`; so far run only with a simulated agent, so it has no results about models yet.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 502c"
      ]
    }
  ]
